  "locks": {},
  "_notes": {
    "flags": "RML-1 is not G-code. The rml logic writes no T word, M6, comment, N word, unit word, coolant word or rotary word, and core/file-validation.json pins each of those flags to false. Multi-tool Roland work is one file per tool, which the multi-file and split-drill exports already produce.",
    "models": "Machine facts per model, read by the rml logic: protocol 'legacy' sets speed with V, 'modern' with !VZ; maxFeedXY and maxFeedZ are mm/s; spindleControl false means no !RC (the machine runs at its own speed); dwell false means no !DW. init starts every program and end closes it. Most models are unverified: check against the machine's manual."
  }
